; ============================================================
; TITLE:    The Chaos Game
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     random, DOT, chaos game, Sierpinski, probability
; SUMMARY:  Plays the chaos game: random jumps halfway to a corner draw a perfect Sierpinski triangle.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Mark three corners. Start anywhere. Again and again, pick a
;   corner at random and jump halfway toward it, leaving a dot. You
;   would expect a mess, but a Sierpinski triangle appears. Each dot
;   gets the color of the corner it jumped toward.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch for a few seconds. Change :jumps or the
;   corners at the bottom.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * DOT to place a single point without moving the turtle
;   * PICK to choose a random item from a list
;   * keeping the current point in two variables
;   * how a random process can still make an exact pattern
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use four corners of a square. Is there a pattern now?
;   * Jump 2/3 of the way instead of halfway (multiply by 0.667).
;   * Use five corners and jump 0.618 of the way for a pentagon.
; ============================================================

; CORNER makes a corner: a list of the point and its color.
to corner :x :y :color
  output (list :x :y :color)
end

; CHAOS plays the game. :ratio is how far each jump goes, 0.5 is half.
to chaos :corners :jumps :ratio
  ; Start at a random point; the first few dots may fall outside the
  ; triangle, but after a dozen jumps the point is always inside.
  localmake "x random 200
  localmake "y random 200
  repeat :jumps [
    localmake "c pick :corners
    ; The brackets around ITEM matter: without them Logo would read
    ; item 1 (:c - :x), because - grabs its neighbors first.
    make "x :x + :ratio * ((item 1 :c) - :x)
    make "y :y + :ratio * ((item 2 :c) - :y)
    if repcount > 12 [
      setpencolor item 3 :c
      dot list :x :y
    ]
  ]
end

; MARK draws a big dot on each corner so you can see the targets.
to mark :corners
  setpensize 12
  foreach :corners [setpencolor item 3 ? dot list item 1 ? item 2 ?]
  setpensize 2
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [20 22 30]
make "corners (list corner 0 280 [255 90 90] ~
                    corner -320 -270 [90 200 255] ~
                    corner 320 -270 [255 220 90])
mark :corners
chaos :corners 15000 0.5
